cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Two cubature rules for the hypercube, with independent verification"
message: "If you use these rules, please cite this repository."
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Chandan
    family-names: Shukla
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-0897-4332"
    affiliation: "Independent researcher"
abstract: >-
  Explicit nodes and weights for two positive interior cubature rules for the
  uniform measure on the hypercube: a 31-node rule of degree 5 on [-1,1]^5,
  which attains Moller's lower bound and is therefore minimal, and a 52-node
  rule of degree 7 on [-1,1]^4. Both have strictly positive weights and all
  nodes strictly interior, and both node sets are centrally symmetric. A
  standard-library checker verifies every monomial of the stated degree against
  exact rational targets, and a second script evaluates Moller's bound. Priority
  against the earlier cubature literature has not been established and no
  novelty is claimed.
keywords:
  - cubature
  - numerical integration
  - hypercube
  - minimal cubature rule
  - Moller bound
